From: Gyimesi Balázs <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nor: macronix: use 4B opcodes on MX25U25635F again

Linux 6.12 still listed the MX25U25635F with SPI_NOR_4B_OPCODES. The
entry is gone since, and the part is left to SFDP. Its SFDP has no
4-byte Address Instruction Table, so the core does not know about the
4B opcodes and switches the flash to 4-byte address mode with EN4B
instead. A warm reset does not leave that mode, the boot ROM reads the
first stage loader with 3-byte addresses and the board hangs. The
TP-Link Archer C2600 stops on every reboot and only comes back after a
power cycle.

Restore the entry with SPI_NOR_4B_OPCODES, which keeps the flash in
3-byte mode. Size and the rest come from SFDP.

Signed-off-by: Gyimesi Balázs <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/macronix.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/macronix.c
@@ -188,6 +188,10 @@
 		.size = SZ_16M,
 		.no_sfdp_flags = SECT_4K | SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ | SPI_NOR_QUAD_READ,
 	}, {
+		/* MX25U25635F */
+		.id = SNOR_ID(0xc2, 0x25, 0x39),
+		.fixup_flags = SPI_NOR_4B_OPCODES,
+	}, {
 		/* MX25U51245G */
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0xc2, 0x25, 0x3a),
 		.fixups = &macronix_qpp4b_fixups,
